<title> Acute Cholecystitis: Management.</title>
<graphic href="eee0174-w0001.gif" />
<cell type="start" id="cell-1">
<label>Acute cholecystitis. Resuscitate, antibiotics, hospital admission. Complicated or unstable?</label>
<path target="cell-2">No</path>
<path target="cell-3">Yes</path>
</cell>
<cell type="action" id="cell-2">
<label>Laparoscopy &lt;72 hours</label>
</cell>
<cell type="decision" id="cell-3">
<label>Perforation or peritonitis?</label>
<path target="cell-4">No</path>
<path target="cell-5">Yes</path>
</cell>
<cell type="decision" id="cell-4">
<label>Contraindication for general anesthesia?</label>
<path target="cell-2">No</path>
<path target="cell-6">Yes</path>
</cell>
<cell type="action" id="cell-6">
<label>Percutaneous cholecystostomy and intravenous antibiotics</label>
</cell>
<cell type="action" id="cell-5">
<label>Laparotomy</label>
</cell>
<footnotes>
<footnote>Adapted from Helton WS, Espat NJ. Cholecystitis and cholangitis. <em>Curr Treat Opt Infect Dis</em> 2001;<strong>3</strong>:387-400.<xref ref="bib42" />
</footnote>
</footnotes>
